\par\par \b \uc2  Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dlr to stem rupee's rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 26 (Reuter) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to halt the rupee's steady rise against the dollar and dealers said it may need to continue buying dollars in the weeks ahead as fears of a rupee depreciation had abated. \par \par \uc2  The rupee closed Friday at 36.19/20 against the dollar, slightly weaker from its 36.18/20 opening, on the back of two rounds of dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "The move was gradual, there was no sharp volatility, but they stepped in nevertheless to stop the rupee's rise," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government said earlier this year that RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed to check excessive volatility and that the exchange rate would be determined by the market. \par \par \uc2  But many dealers were unsure whether this was the case. \par \par \uc2  "They did not buy (dollars) yesterday when the rupee rose by ten paise," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had been speculating about RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the rupee breached the 36.30-mark, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars last Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Friday at 36.18/20 compared to the previous close of 36.16/17, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The morning session saw mild dollar demand, with some trades at 36.20/22 per dollar levels. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales by some Delhi-based banks, notably a Japanese bank, triggered an appreciation in the rupee which was only arrested by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI stepped in when the rupee hit a high of 36.175 and stepped up its purchases up to 36.20 levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee began rising again in the afternoon session and towards the close RBI bought dollars from a string of public sector banks in Bombay, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Continued foreign direct and portfolio investment and foreign equity issues planned by public sector Indian firms would exert upward pressure on the rupee in coming months, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment firm Merrill Lynch said on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks in India were lower given the Indian rupee's resilience and stronger fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "We expect that any weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be limited given that the Indian rupee at 36.2 rupees to a dollar is already close to our fair value estimate of 37.2," it said. \par \par \uc2  Merrill Lynch said low inflation and declining interest rates make the Indian stock market a favoured destination for investment in the Asian region, excluding Japan. \par \par \uc2  Merrill Lynch has recommended increasing its asset allocation in Indian markets. \par \par \uc2  "In India, our views on sharply declining long term interest rates, benign inflation, continued economic reform and attractive valuations underpin our overweight stance," it said. \par \par \uc2  "With expectations of earnings growth of 15 percent in FY98 (financial year ending March 31) and 18 percent in FY99, India is a favourite market in Asia, ex-Japan," it added. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom (91)22-265 9000, Fax 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9q01vou\par }\p