\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends down after RBI buys dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 26 (Reuter) - Two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) to arrest the rupee's rise pulled the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a slightly lower close on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Their (RBI's) ways are inscrutable," said a dealer, referring to gradual appreciation of the rupee this week. \par \par \uc2  "The move was gradual, there was no sharp volatility, but they stepped in nevertheless to stop the rupee's rise." \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been speculating about possible RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever since the rupee breached the 36.30-mark, the level at which it bought dollars last Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened Friday at 36.18/20 compared to the previous close of 36.16/17, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The morning session saw mild dollar demand, with transactions at 36.20/22 levels. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales by some Delhi-based banks, notably a Japanese bank, triggered a rise in the rupee which was ultimately arrested by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI stepped in when the rupee hit a high of 36.175 and stepped up its purchases upto 36.20 levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "They did not buy (dollars) yesterday when the rupee rose by ten paise," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee began rising again and towards the close RBI bought dollars from a string of public sector banks in Bombay, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The forward market was dull and volumes were thin, dealers said. The six month forward premium closed Friday at 5.60 percent against 6.04 percent previous close. \par \par \uc2  ---Bombay Newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax 22-264 1699 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9q01voa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
