\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends sharply up v dlr as RBI watches. \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 25 (Reuter) - The rupee ended sharply up against the dollar on Thursday at 36.16/17 against 36.265/275 opening and the previous close of 36.25/26, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee gained 10 paise from 36.26 per dollar in early morning trade to 36.16 towards the close, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers kept a shary eye out for Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupee broke below the 36.20 level in afternoon trade, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept away. \par \par \uc2  Importer covering stalled the rupee briefly at 36.20, but the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon broke through. \par \par \uc2  "RBI made enquiries after it slipped the 36.20-mark, prompting fresh bidding at 36.200/205 level," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But when banks realised the RBI was confining itself to enquiries, fresh dollar selling began, and the rupee marched through to 36.17, with a few stray deals at 36.16, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Taking a view on the rupee in effect means taking a view on the RBI," a chief dealer at a Bombay ban remarked. \par \par \uc2  "There were good inward (dollar) remittances today," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "And no one wanted to go long on dollars today for technical reasons," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said cash spot and cash tomorrow rates will open higher as Friday deals are for October 1 spot value. \par \par \uc2  Banks are closed on September 30 for an half-yearly closing of accounts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the rupee to make  fresh gains on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sharukh Wadia, chief dealer at Standard Chartered Bank, said he expected the rupee to open around 36.19/20 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "If the RBI does not step in, it (the dollar) could drift to 36.15 level," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee wekened slightly on importer covering in a dull forward market, dealers said. The six month annualised forward premium closed at 6.04, compared to Wednesday's close of 5.87 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom (91)22-265 9000, Fax 22 264 1699 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9p021zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
