\par\par \b \uc2  RBI's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  warning pushes up Delhi shares. \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, Sept 11 (Reuter) - Delhi shares gained in early trade on Thursday as foreign investors, encouraged by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warning against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, made selective purchases, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The Delhi bourse's Sensitive Index was up 3.62 points at 849.08 after 30 minutes of trade. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement that it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market brought back confidence among foreign investors," Sushil Jain of Jain Finance and Securities said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, RBI Governor C. Rangarajan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the spot and forward rupee markets to reduce exchange rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened at 36.54/58 per dollar on Thursday against Wednesday's close of 36.53/55. \par \par \uc2  Hindustan Lever, which powered the Delhi market higher on Wednesday, added five rupees to 1,440. \par \par \uc2  Reliance Industries gained 0.20 rupee to 343. \par \par \uc2  TISCO added 2.30 rupees to 188 on short-covering and speculative buying. \par \par \uc2  State Bank of India firmed 2.60 rupees to 288.50 on foreign buying. \par \par \uc2  ITC gained six rupees to 558. \par \par \uc2  -- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9b02qjl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\