\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  RBI to continue  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 -governor. \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 10 (Reuter) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to check volatility, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chakravarty Rangarajan said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  both in the spot and forward markets to reduce volatility and to ensure orderly conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Rangarajan said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "The recent volatility seen in the exchange rate has been caused in a large measure by the rush to cover unhedged positions. There has been no basic change in the fundamentals of the economy which continue to remain strong." \par \par \uc2  "Market participants both in the spot and forward markets are, therefore, advised to take note of the basic trends," the governor said. \par \par \uc2  He said the fundamentals of the economy, especially in relation to the external sector, were unchanged and are strong. \par \par \uc2  "The current account deficit has remained low and it is estimated to be at 1.4 percent of GDP for 1996/97. It is not likely to exceed 1.5 percent in 1997/98," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said capital flows under various routes -- non-resident deposits, portfolio investment, direct investments and external commercial borrowings -- are steady and strong. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased by $5.2 billion in 1996/97 and by a further $4.0 billion in the current financial year till the end of August 1997, the governor said. \par \par \uc2  He said the rupee had depreciated against the dollar in the last two weeks after a prolonged period of stability. \par \par \uc2  "The depreciation is of the order of 2.5 percent. At the present level, the rupee depreciation in relation to the dollar is far less than in the case of East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which have experienced unusual turbulence," he said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI later clarified that the current account deficit during 1996/97 is estimated at 1.0 percent of GDP and not 1.4 percent as earlier stated. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom (91)22-265 9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt9a003sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
