\par\par \b \uc2  India must allow rupee to respond to market - IMF. \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, Sept 10 (Reuter) - The International Monetary Fund (IMF) on Wednesday urged India to allow its exchange rate to respond to market signals. \par \par \uc2  The annual report of IMF's executive board for the financial year ending April 30, said that its directors had stressed the need for India to have a flexible exchange rate management in close coordination with other macroeconomic variables. \par \par \uc2  A senior IMF official in New Delhi also said that India must move in a phased manner towards full rupee convertibility. \par \par \uc2  "They stressed that the exchange rate should be allowed to respond to market signals and that in managing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the authorities should avoid a too mechanical reliance on indicators of the real exchange rate," the IMF report said. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to smoothen any fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee ended on Monday at a 19-month low, but the RBI cushioned the fall by selling dollars before the market moved too fast, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee closed at 36.685/95 per dollar on Monday, after opening unchanged at 36.57/59. Spot rupee on Tuesday closed at 36.59/61 against the dollar compared with 36.60/72 opening and 36.68/69 closing, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had held steady against the dollar at 35.70/85 for nearly a year until the mid-August watershed. \par \par \uc2  But it had appreciated on its real effective exchange rate index -- which takes into account inflation differentials against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concern. \par \par \uc2  Deputy RBI Governor Y.V. Reddy told a meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers last month that the rupee is overvalued in light of an analysis of Real Effective Exchange Rate (REER) data. \par \par \uc2  IMF would focus on including capital account convertibility in its articles of agreement at its annual meeting to be held later this month in Hong Kong, the IMF official said. \par \par \uc2  "The Fund has decided that capital account convertibility in appropriate circumstances can add to world economic growth and an individual country's prosperity," the IMF official, who asked not to be identified, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "It has benefits for India but has to be in a phased manner," he said. \par \par \uc2  A panel appointed by the RBI in June submitted its recommendations to make the rupee convertible by the turn of the century. \par \par \uc2  But the IMF official said India must restructure its state-owned banks before getting to capital account convertibility. \par \par \uc2  "There are many weak banks and it is difficult to see how they survive under competition," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt9a003lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
