\par\par \b \uc2  RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  slows Indian rupee depreciation. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Sept 9 (Reuter) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (RBI) daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market aims to ensure its overvalued rupee depreciates smoothly rather than to turn the tide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has fallen by over two percent since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  labelled its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overvalued in mid-August. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 19-month low of 36.72 per dollar, but rallied after the RBI sold up to $120 million and closed at 36.59/61 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Some bankers said it was a correction. "The rupee was falling too much and too fast," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI is probably not averse to seeing the rupee further down - maybe around 37.50 by end March. But the problem is, the market is looking to take it there straightaway," he said. \par \par \uc2  "So the RBI is just cooling things down by dollar selling." \par \par \uc2  "The interbank market was long on dollars," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "When RBI sold early in the morning, stop-loss limits were breached and longs were quickly unwound." \par \par \uc2  He said the overall view on the rupee remained bearish. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had held steady against the dollar at 35.70/85 for nearly a year until the mid-August watershed. \par \par \uc2  But it had appreciated on its real effective exchange rate index -- which takes into account inflation differentials against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concern. \par \par \uc2  However, having given the green light to sell rupees, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to act to stop a precipitous fall. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to pilot the rupee to around 37 rupees per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think RBI is helping a soft-landing to 37 (rupees to a dollar) level," Ravi Kumar, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ABN-AMRO Bank N.V. in Bombay told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  This week, RBI began selling dollars at 36.65 rupees on Monday before stepping up the price to 36.685 and on Tuesday sold at 36.72. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many Indian exporters had cancelled forward dollar sales, increasing nervousness among Indian firms needing to cover forward dollar commitments. \par \par \uc2  A horde of Indian firms who raised offshore loans and did not take forward cover as the rupee held steady against the dollar until August have now rushed to cover, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Indian exporters have been complaining that the overvalued rupee was one of the main reasons for the deceleration in India's export growth in 1997/98 (April-March). \par \par \uc2  HSBC Markets said a weaker rupee would act as a deterrent for imports. The government has been seeking to kickstart corporate activity - a weaker rupee would not help it. \par \par \uc2  A strong rupee has been blamed for a deceleration in Indian export growth this year. But latest numbers show April-July exports rose 1.81 percent to $11.03 billion from a year earlier, and July exports rose 6.64 pct to $2.77 billion from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt99001iw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
