\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 : RBI Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Volatility - Fin Min \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par 15:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The market will determine the daily value of the rupee, but high volatility and speculative attacks will be countered by the Reserve Bank of India, Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said in an interview, according to a local news agency Friday. \par \par \uc2  Chidambaram said the government doesn't approve of volatility or speculative activity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to a Press Trust of India report. \par \par \uc2  'The value of the rupee will be determined by the market,' Chidambaram was reported to have said. 'But the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent volatility and speculative activity. We don't approve of volatility. We don't approve of speculative activity. Otherwise it will be market determined.' \par \par \uc2  The interview came amid a turbulent period on India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the rupee weakened on a newspaper report, later denied, that the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were planning to set a trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at around 35.70 rupees on Aug. 19 but later strengthened to an 18-month high of 36.50 rupees on the report. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 36.36 rupees Wednesday, the last trading day since a two-day bank strike closed the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-08-97 \par \par