\par\par \b \uc2  India/Rupee -2: Sudden Depreciation Was Unexpected \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1997\par 16:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  An expert committee of the RBI headed by former Deputy Governor S.S. Tarapore on June 3 recommended that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fix a trading band for the rupee of 5.0% on either side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's neutral real effective exchange rate, adjusted for inflation and trade. \par \par \uc2  The panel had suggested that the RBI shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee was trading within the band except to curb speculation and volatility. \par \par \uc2  The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under tremendous upward pressure against the dollar, due mainly to large inflows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from international investors. The RBI has been buying dollars steadily to keep the rupee from appreciating in a bid to protect the competitiveness of Indian exports. By Aug. 8, its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets were up $3.83 billion from March 31. \par \par \uc2  That still hasn't been enough to cap the rupee's rise and meet exporters' demand for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the RBI is constrained by the effect of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on domestic monetary targets. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's M3 measure of broad money supply was up 16.7% year-on-year on July 18, against a target of growth of between 15% and 15.5% for the financial year ending March 31, 1998. \par \par \uc2  'We had expected a steady depreciation of the rupee to that level, but this is much faster than anticipated,' said Rajan Govil, economist at HSBC Batliwala & Karani Securities (Holding) Pvt. Ltd. 'I see the dollar at 37.80 rupees by end-March.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1403GMT \par \par \uc2  1194 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8l067dl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
