\par\par \b \uc2  INDIAN RUPEE ENDS UP, FORWARD DLR PREMIUMS FALL. \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 7 (Reuter) - The forward dollar premiums fell on Thursday but the spot rupee ended up at 35.7050/7150 despite Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar opened the day steady at 35.715/725 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said premiums fell sharply on forward dollar sales at higher levels. \par \par \uc2  "Besides, quite a few traders had booked forwards anticipating the RBI will buy forward dollars and push premiums up," said a public sector bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  This did not happen. One banker said he heard RBI bought January dollars towards the close of the market but other banks could not confirm RBI's forward dollar purchases on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The forward market saw profit-booking and loss cutting today," said the chief dealer at a public sector bank. \par \par \uc2  "In a perfect market, spot rate and premiums will move in tandem and adjust according to interest rate differentials," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Indian market being imperfect, only forward premiums rose on large RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week even as the spot rupee gained against the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI succeeded in creating some volatility and panic among those with dollar liabilities -- importers and those with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan exposure," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the spot section, there was little demand for dollars except from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The RBI began buying at 35.7175 and later brought down the price to 35.7150 and finally to 35.7125, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The six month annualised forward premium closed Thursday at 4.59 percent compared to the previous close of 5.04 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8701i1n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
