\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Steady Against Dollar At Mid-Morning \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1997\par 06:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee opened unchanged against the dollar Tuesday and continues to trade in its opening range, mostly around 35.7400 rupees, with banks cautious and buying some dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There is some dollar demand in early trading because banks are buying dollars on expectation that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later Tuesday to boost the dollar-rupee exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened between 35.7350 rupees and 35.7450 rupees Tuesday, unchanged from its close on Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0405 GMT (12:05 a.m. EDT), the dollar is trading, within the opening range, between 35.7375 rupees 35.7425 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had closed Friday between 35.7700 rupees and 35.7800 rupees, up sharply from its Thursday close of between 35.7100 rupees and 35.7150 rupees on forward dollar purchases by the RBI. \par \par \uc2  The RBI once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday by buying forward dollars but the spot-dollar-rupee exchange rate closed lower between 35.735 rupees and 35.745 rupees Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said this was because of more than enough dollar inflows from foreign investments and Indian companies raising foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans from the international market. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI is expected to keep the pressure on the rupee by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward dollar market,' said a dealer at a large state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  He explained that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by being in a overbought position in the forward dollar across maturities over the next one year will be able to hold the spot-dollar-rupee exchange rate at the current levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months has been buying dollars to keep the rupee from appreciating against the rupee to protect Indian exports. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to range between 35.7300 rupees and 35.7800 rupees for the rest of the trading session Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  For the latest rupee indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [17960]. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES INDIA REPORT  05-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0432GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt8501267\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
