\par\par \b \uc2  India RBI pulls down rupee against forward dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 4 (Reuter) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the forward dollar market on Monday, pushing up forward premiums, even as the commerce minister said the rupee's appreciation against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was affecting Indian export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  RBI's purchases pushed up premiums by almost 10 paise for January dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  January dollars were quoted at 77/80 paise on Monday evening compared to the opening level of 69/70, they said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought forward dollars across wide maturities -- January, April and June, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  RBI also repeatedly hit the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Large dollar sales by a handful of foreign banks -- estimated at $150 million -- made RBI's spot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ineffective, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  These banks were selling the proceeds of a $150 million FRN raised by Indian Railway Finance Corp, the funding arm of Indian Railways, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot dollar was at 35.732/740 rupees in latest quotes compared with 35.77/79, they said. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265  9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8401kkw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
