\par\par \b \uc2  India's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  knocks rupee to one-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 1 (Reuter) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rode a wave of changing sentiment towards the rupee on Friday, buying dollars in the open market to knock the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to one-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rupee dropped briefly below 35.82 to the dollar after heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) combined with import-related dollar buying and covering of short positions in the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  By the close of business it was at 35.78/79 against the dollar after starting at 35.705/710. \par \par \uc2  "It's a combination of factors...RBI buying, import covering, some interbank short-covering," one dealer at a foreign bank in Bombay. "It looks like sentiment has changed, we saw some import covering today for the near months after quite some time." \par \par \uc2  The RBI, unlike beleaguered central banks in Southeast Asia, has been struggling for the past year with a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to heavy inflows of foreign funds and weak import demand. \par \par \uc2  In the past 12 months it has appreciated by around seven percent. \par \par \uc2  In recent days the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had successfully capped the rupee at 35.70 per dollar, dipping into the market openly or -- to keep the traders guessing -- simply buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from banks whenever they offered them for sale. \par \par \uc2  India's authorities are worried that persistent rupee strength could dent exports, which tend to be price-sensitive. \par \par \uc2  The Commerce Ministry reported on Friday that exports fell 0.95 percent in the first quarter of the financial year beginning April from the same period a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the drop could be linked to depressed global markets and infrastructure bottlenecks which hold up industrial growth shared the blame along with the rising rupee. \par \par \uc2  "With the appreciation of the rupee and depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the surrounding countries there will be some anxieties among the exporters," said V. Raghuraman, Secretary General of the Associated Chambers of Commerce. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8101r55\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
