\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee on tight-rope walk on RBI dlr buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, July 23 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee traded precariously at 35.69/70 against the dollar on Wednesday as the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  'passively' to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee closed the day at 35.69/70 against the opening quote of 35.702/707, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The day's range was 35.6975 to 35.7075, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The day began with trades at 35.7050 rupees to a dollar on expectations of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the rupee started edging up as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not show up, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the RBI was 'passively' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying dollars at 35.70-level from several banks which approached it, they said. \par \par \uc2  But for this passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupee would have appreciated against the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has appreciated against the dollar in recent months on large capital inflows and lack of strong import demand. Foreign institutional investment (FII) in Indian stock markets continued after a brief slowdown, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Net FII purchases on the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) on July 21 amounted to 150 million rupees, according to latest BSE data. \par \par \uc2  The forward dollar market saw some paying interest (payment of premiums for purchase of forward dollars), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The six-month annualised premium closed at 3.52 percent, up from the previous close of 3.47 percent, they said.