\par\par \b \uc2  India/RBI Buys Dollars -2: Small Amount Of Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par 11:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of India bought dollars for rupees at mid-afternoon Wednesday when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading between 35.6975 rupees and 35.7075 rupees, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI started buying dollars around 35.7000 rupees and is currently buying the dollars up to 35.7100 rupees,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank that sold to RBI. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought in lots of $5.0 million, she said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI purchased between $30 to $50 million, a dealer at a European bank that sold to the RBI estimated. This is a relatively modest amount for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The RBI dollar buying pushed the dollar to between 35.7100 and 35.7125 rupees at around 0945 GMT (5:45 a.m. EDT), said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker. \par \par \uc2  And dealers said the State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank, is now buying dollars at around 35.7100 rupees. \par \par \uc2  The RBI is believed to support the dollar above the 35.7000 rupees mark, rather than letting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken against the rupee, which would hurt Indian exporters. \par \par \uc2  This is the fourth consecutive trading session in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  REPORT  16-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0959GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected at 11:56GMT) \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt7g00z59\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
