\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee strength bucks regional trend. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Simon Cameron-Moore \par \uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, July 15 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee is bursting with strength, undaunted by either the dollar's supremacy against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a domino-effect collapse among south-east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers and analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Waves of portfolio investment have poured into Asia's best-performing stock market in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The Bombay stock index is up almost 30 percent from January 1, striking 33-month highs last week, and because of the rupee's strength the profile looks even stronger. There has also been a regular stream of foreign direct investment (FDI). \par \par \uc2  "The reason the rupee's been so strong is the steady inflow of foreign funds and weak import demand," said Nupur Joshi, economist at Jardine Fleming (\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Broking Ltd. \par \par \uc2  "And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as actively as it can." \par \par \uc2  While other central banks around south and south-east Asia are either actively devaluing or battling against tumbling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank of India has struggled to keep the rupee on a tight rein. \par \par \uc2  The RBI, along with India's largest state-owned commercial bank, State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dominates \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  is causing a growing problem for the RBI, which has to neutralise the growth in money supply caused by selling rupees for dollars. \par \par \uc2  India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves totalled $25.4 billion in June, compared with $17.3 billion a year ago. \par \par \uc2  Portfolio investment inflows and FDI amounted to $5.0 billion in 1996/97 (April-March). And since April portfolio investment inflows have totaled around $700 million. There are no reliable figures for FDI inflows this fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  Add to this the herd of Indian corporates raising foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans abroad. The flood of money coming in will test the RBI's ability to contain the rupee for much longer. \par \par \uc2  About $50 billion is traded in rupee-dollar transactions each month, according to RBI estimates. \par \par \uc2  The power of inflows is likely to get greater as India moves towards a capital account convertibility. The rupee is presently convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  An unexpected absence of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the rupee to break below 35.70 to the dollar on Friday, marking its strongest level for seven months. It finished Tuesday around 35.71, after the RBI came in again to sell rupees. \par \par \uc2  On its real effective exchange rate (REER) the rupee has appreciated by around seven percent in the last 12 months, analysts said. The RBI does not publish its REER index on a daily basis, so uptodate, precise calculations are difficult. \par \par \uc2  India's rung further down the development ladder puts the rupee in a different cycle from south-east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "India is an emerging market, not an Asian market," said Mark McFarland, economist at Peregrine Brokerage Ltd in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  South East Asian countries are well established on their development paths, while India is coming from a lot further back, analysts said. Liberal economic reforms began in India in 1991, but have regained impetus in the last year under the stewardship of Finance Minister P.Chidamabaram. \par \par \uc2  "India is different because it is just liberalising. The inflows of foreign capital are linked to the changes in policy it is nothing to do with arbitraging interest rates or anything like that," Mcfarland said. \par \par \uc2  That drive towards reform have put India further along the track than its South Asian competitors, Bangladesh, Pakistan and Sri Lanka. All three countries \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have weakened either through pegged devaluations or slowly guided depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence with its neighbours will hit India's exports, which are, software sector apart, low value added and price sensitive, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Ravi Kumar, chief dealer at ABN-AMRO Bank in Bombay said a strong rupee to pay for capital imports and to build the home market made abundant sense, even if the export sector suffered. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7f02k0u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
