\par\par \b \uc2  India/RBI Buys Dollars -2: Small Amount Of Dollar-Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1997\par 12:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of India bought U.S. dollars for rupees Tuesday when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading around 35.7050 rupees, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI is buying the dollar around 35.7050 rupees,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank, who confirmed selling dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers at a few other foreign banks who confirmed selling the dollar to the RBI said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made only small amounts of dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  However, the RBI dollar purchases pushed the dollar up to trade between 35.7100 rupees and 35.7200 rupees at the close of interbank trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI started buying dollars at around 35.7050 rupees just 10 minutes before the close of trading, and continued to purchase until around 35.7100 rupees,' said a dealer at a private bank. \par \par \uc2  The RBI is seen as keen to keep the dollar above the 35.7000-rupee mark, rather than let the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken against the rupee, which would hurt Indian exporters. \par \par \uc2  This is the third consecutive trading session in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  REPORT  15-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1053GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt7f00yct\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal