\par\par \b \uc2  Strong global dollar bends before the Indian rupee. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shyam Kumar \par \uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, July 14 (Reuter) - The U.S. dollar, surging against major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was fighting a losing battle against the Indian rupee on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended the day a shade weaker after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, buying dollars to push the rupee to close at 35.72/73 against a 35.71/72 opening. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had closed at the latter level on Friday after the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through the crucial 35.70-mark to trade at 35.69. \par \par \uc2  The market was looking to the RBI from early Monday morning but dollar purchases by the State Bank of India (SBI), India's largest bank, helped hold the dollar at the 35.71/72 level. \par \par \uc2  SBI's dollar purchases usually move the thin Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  After SBI withdrew from the market, the rupee eased to 35.7050/7100, threatening to test the 35.70-barrier, provoking RBI's entry, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  RBI bought unspecified amounts of dollars upto the 35.73 level, dealers said. On Friday too, RBI purchases had pushed the rupee to 35.72/73 before closing at 35.71/72, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The (dollar) supplies were heavy today," said the treasurer of a European bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  India's leading truck maker Tata Engineering and Locomotive Company is raising $200 million in overseas debt and two Indian telecommunications firms are about to begin road shows to tap the global capital market. \par \par \uc2  Foreign institutional investors (FII) continue their purchases on Indian bourses. On July 10, FIIs' net purchases on the Bombay Stock Exchange alone amounted to 80 million rupees, according to latest data released by the exchange. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI has decided to put the dollar on '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  oxygen' only in extreme cases," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Indian exporters have been crying themselves hoarse about an overvalued rupee hurting their competitiveness but the government is helpless in the face of unabated capital flows into the country, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has become a graveyard for dealers," said a dealer at a European bank in Bombay. "If the fundamentals are so strong, they should allow the rupee to strengthen," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Otherwise the RBI should open a dollar purchase window," he said. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current unannounced \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  left most banks groping in the dark. \par \par \uc2  "Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not help anyone," he said. \par \par \uc2  The six month annualised forward dollar premium closed the day at 3.52 percent, down from the previous close of 3.63 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02qn1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
