\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's RBI  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to halt rupee surge vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, July 11 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee softened on Friday after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains but it remained around its strongest level for seven months against the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In mid-afternoon trade, the rupee was quoted at 35.705/712 per dollar after touching 35.69 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI bought dollars and weakened the rupee after the unit broke a key level. \par \par \uc2  "I think the RBI decided to step in once the rupee breached 35.70," said the chief dealer at a European bank. "The rupee was on a one-way trip upwards till the RBI came in. But they bought in small amounts...looks like they only wanted to make an appearance." \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the rupee touched its strongest level in seven months of 35.735 against the dollar, after opening at 35.755/765, on poor dollar demand and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  inaction. \par \par \uc2  The RBI's absence from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday triggered speculation on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would check the rupee's gains or let market forces determine the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The Business Standard daily said on Friday that the RBI had decided not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless there was an "extreme provocation". \par \par \uc2  The decision was made after a meeting between RBI governor Chakravarty Rangarajan and finance minister P. Chidambaram last Saturday, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  An RBI spokesperson declined to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  The spokesperson said the RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was guided by the demand-supply situation in the market and it sought to even out any mismatches. \par \par \uc2  The other objective was to keep the value of the rupee close to the real effective exchange rate, the spokesperson added. \par \par \uc2  Indian exporters have in recent months been complaining about the exchange rate, saying the rupee was overvalued and its strength would affect their competitiveness in international markets. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, neighbouring Pakistan devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the move was a technical correction to adjust for the U.S. dollar's appreciation against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worldwide. \par \par \uc2  Indian exports grew only four percent to $33.1 billion in 1996/97 (April-March) compared to 21.4 percent growth the previous year. \par \par \uc2  "Part of the reason for the rupee's rise since yesterday is that some banks were holding long dollar positions," said a dealer. "The general market expectation was that RBI would buy dollars at 35.75 and check the rupee's rise but this didn't happen." \par \par \uc2  "Banks were forced to unwind their longs on Thursday when the RBI didn't come in as the rupee hit 35.75," he said. \par \par \uc2  "There was no sign of the RBI today till (the) afternoon and this again led to selling. In recent times the only demand has been from RBI," he said. \par \par \uc2  "When they are away, even normal supplies do not get absorbed by the market and push the rupee up." \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been buoyant for the past year due to healthy inflows of dollars supply and poor demand for the U.S. unit. Inflows have been mainly from foreign investment and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings by Indian corporates. \par \par \uc2  India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves leapt to $25.4 billion on June 27 from $19.7 billion on February 28. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7b02oit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
