\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee/Closes -2: RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely Thursday \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1997\par 13:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar will strengthen only if the Reserve Bank of India buys dollars. They said this will happen if the exchange rate falls below 35.75 rupees. \par \par \uc2  'I see reason to believe that RBI will buy dollars Thursday or Friday and (dollar) rates will start looking up after that,' a dealer with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  But, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar could fall well below 35.75 rupees soon as supplies of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appear to be high, he said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, in the overnight interbank money market, call rates continued to fall with excess money supply keeping the rate down in spite of some demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rate closed between 2.00% and 2.75%, down from 2.75% and 3.25% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the call rate will remain low for the rest of the week, although the rate will be affected by the outcome of an auction of four-day repurchase agreements for government securities by the Reserve Bank Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At a previous three-day repo auction Monday, the RBI accepted four bids for 45.00 billion rupees at a cut-off yield 3.90%. This was lower than expected by some analysts. \par \par \uc2  For the latest call money indicative rates, please see Dow Jones Markets page [57435]. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1145GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt79053q4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\p