\par\par \b \uc2  India money supply gets priority over rupee - RBI. \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BASLE, Switzerland, June 9 (Reuter) - Controlling money supply growth is more crucial to \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  than the exchange rate, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold back the strong rupee can be sustained, Reserve Bank of India (RBI) deputy governor Y.V. Reddy said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Asked where the RBI's priority lay between money supply growth and the rupee rate, Reddy said the former held the key. \par \par \uc2  "Money supply is naturally the dominant factor that we have to keep in view," he told Reuters Financial Television while attending the annual meeting of the Bank for International Settlements in Basle. \par \par \uc2  "If the money supply goes out of hand then it will ultimately result in inflation and exchange rate distortions -- so they are not separate in that sense," he said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI has a 15.0-15.5 M3 monetary growth target. Latest M3 data, on May 9, showed growth running at 16.3 pct year on year. \par \par \uc2  Heavy RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars and selling rupees, has raised worries that domestic monetary growth could surge unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sterilises the inflow of rupees through sales of government debt. \par \par \uc2  Reddy said the RBI had managed to do this successfully in 1996/7 (April-March) and could do so again if needed. \par \par \uc2  "Last year actually we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and mopped up more than $5.0 billion and managed with a money supply of just 15.6 percent." \par \par \uc2  "And in the first two months of this year (April-May) we have already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...(to the tune of) $2.0 billion," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It just shows that we can do that and we may have to continue to do that," he added. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was trading at 35.78 to the dollar on Monday morning in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  Reddy said the RBI had a large enough stock of government debt to sell, but this would have to be combined with other measures to sterlise any sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on the right track for capital account convertibility, as mapped out in a report by a committee appointed by the RBI which was published last week. \par \par \uc2  He also said he did not see any particular reason for a rapid moderation in foreign capital inflows into India after they doubled to $6.5 billion in 1996/7. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt69048n0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
