\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 /RBI Buying -2: RBI Source Denies  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par 08:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars for rupees Tuesday when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading between 35.8150 rupees and 35.8300 rupees, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But at 0600 GMT (2:00 a.m. EDT) a source at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as yet. He refused to confirm whether any banks went and offered dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank and another dealer at a European bank confirmed selling dollars to the RBI. \par \par \uc2  But a dealer at another U.S. bank said the State Bank of India, a large commercial bank, was the major buyer of the dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He said the State Bank started making significant dollar purchases from around 0530 GMT (1:30 EDT) which mainly pushed up the dollar-rupee exchange rate briefly to a high of 35.8300 rupees. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at State Bank refused to comment on its dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  As reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for rupees Monday. \par \par \uc2  The RBI is perceived as keen to keep the dollar-rupee exchange rate around current levels, rather than letting the dollar weaken against the rupee, which would hurt Indian exporters. \par \par \uc2  At 0615 GMT (2:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at 35.8150 rupees and 35.8250 rupees, higher from 35.7850 rupees and 35.7950 at the opening Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they see the dollar trading between 35.8000-35.8300 rupees for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES INDIA REPORT  27-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0624GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt5r00sac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
