\par\par \b \uc2  India says market can set rupee rate, within limits. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, May 12 (Reuter) - Judging by Indian monetary authorities' words and action \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders can play with the rupee anywhere between 35.75-90 per dollar, albeit under the watchful eye of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis within that range, but as soon as the 35.75 level is neared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying become heavier, they said. \par \par \uc2  Both the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) governor Chakaravaty Rangarajan and Finance Minister Palaniappen Chidambaram have said the market should set the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  But only regular \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped the rupee firming sharply. Chidambaram spelt out the RBI strategy in an interview with Reuters Financial Television on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  indiscriminately," the Finance Minister said. "Within a band it allows the rupee to fluctuate and it's only when it goes beyond the band does the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The RBI's recent forays into the market have signalled how far the market can go. \par \par \uc2  "I think a 35.75-35.90 range seems to be indicated if you look at the two levels of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer. "They (RBI) stepped in when the rupee looked like breaking 35.75 but allowed the market to find its own level back from 35.89." \par \par \uc2  In late trade Monday, the rupee was quoted 35.835/842, against 35.840/845 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one-way at the moment. Poor dollar demand and strong supply will keep the rupee buoyant in the near term and only the RBI can stem its rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment the only demand is from the RBI," said a dealer at a state-run bank. "Left to itself, the rupee can only appreciate." \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said the situation was ideal for building up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, currently equivalent to seven months imports at $26.65 billion, ahead of an end goal of full convertibility. \par \par \uc2  Exporters have been asking for a depreciation in the rupee against the dollar, complaining that its strength is undermining their competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also reckoned that the rupee should depreciate by anywhere between three and six percent annually to reflect inflation and other economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  But Chidambaram said on Sunday the rupee was currently at the right level and the market should set the rate. \par \par \uc2  "No, I do not think we should induce a depreciation just to boost someone's confidence," Chidambaram said in reply to a question whether the rupee should be weakened. \par \par \uc2  "Once you say the rupee will find its level in the market, then you must leave it to the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has traded in a broad 35.75-35.90 per dollar range since last July. In recent weeks it has threatened to break through the 35.75 barrier but was blocked by RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI bought $400-500 million last week to push the rupee down to its current levels from last Monday's opening of 35.75. RBI purchases weakened the rupee to 35.89 on Wednesday before it rallied to current levels. \par \par \uc2  (c