\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus: India Rupee Seen Set For A Fall \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jyoti Pande \par \uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1997\par 11:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--Currently considered overvalued against the dollar, the Indian rupee is poised to fall about 3% to 5% later this year, economists and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Some predict the rupee may drop sharply, as it did in late 1995 and early 1996, when speculative forces hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after two years of stability. \par \par \uc2  Others suggest that the fall may be more gradual, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking the lead in nudging the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower toward its fundamental level, seen by some around 36.5 rupees per dollar. \par \par \uc2  But there's a general consensus the rupee will fall, as the current overvaluation is unsustainable in the longer term. Economists say the rupee needs to weaken against the dollar to make exports more competitive - exports in the fiscal year ended March 31, 1997 grew by around 4%, well down from growth of almost 21% in the previous fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar currently trades around 35.865 rupees, down a touch from 35.89 rupees at the end of 1996. \par \par \uc2  A recent report by DSP-Merrill Lynch warned of a heightened 'probability of a sharp depreciation in the future. \par \par \uc2  The report argues that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less actively in coming months to prevent the rupee's appreciation. Without active \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupee is expected to remain overvalued in the near term, setting it up for a sharp fall later in the year, the report stated, as an overvalued rupee isn't sustainable over a longer period. \par \par \uc2  'In such a scenario, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to fall below the fundamental levels on speculative pressure, before recovering on active RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' it predicts. \par \par \uc2  Despite annual inflation of 6%-8% over the past few months, the rupee has held steady against the dollar in recent months, even as the dollar rose sharply against many other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That suggests an overvaluation on an underlying real exchange rate basis. The rupee has been supported by large capital inflows from external commercial borrowing, by issues of Global Depository Receipts by Indian companies and foreign investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0918GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5803ami\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
