\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 /RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Steady Dollar Buyer \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1997\par 07:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (AP-Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of India bought dollars for rupees Wednesday when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading between 35.8725 rupees and 35.8825 rupees, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0520 GMT (1:20 a.m. EDT), dealers at banks who confirmed selling the dollars to the RBI said the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars at around 35.8750 rupees. \par \par \uc2  They said the RBI made steady purchases of the dollar from a level of around 35.8550 rupees earlier Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The volume of the dollar purchases made by the RBI wasn't immediately clear. \par \par \uc2  As a matter of policy, the RBI doesn't officially comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The RBI is perceived as keen to keep the dollar-rupee exchange rate around current levels, rather than letting the dollar weaken against the rupee, which would hurt Indian exporters. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a British bank who sold dollars to the RBI said the dollar will rise to around 35.95 rupees if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to buy dollars. He said the RBI isn't comfortable with seeing the rupee appreciate further against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Wednesday between 35.8350 rupees and 35.8450 rupees, but soon climbed to 35.8600 rupees on strong buying interest from commercial banks. Dealers said banks had anticipated that the RBI would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, and were hoping to sell the dollars they purchased early in the day to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a profit. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0544GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt57039qe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
