\par\par \b \uc2  India: Rupee Premium On Forward Dollars Slightly Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 07:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The premiums in the forward market for the dollar are slightly higher in Bombay interbank trading Thursday because of buying of forward dollars by banks on behalf of importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a U.S. bank said the premium for dollars to be delivered at the end of September is between 1.30 rupees and 1.32 rupees. The premium closed Wednesday between 1.29 rupees and 1.31 rupees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there isn't much activity in the forward market, but importers are cautious and buying some forward dollars because of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday afternoon bought forward dollars for delivery at the end of March and the end of May, before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market near the close of trading. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar is trading between 35.845 rupees and 35.855 rupees at 0545 GMT (12:45 a.m. EST), slightly down from the opening because of the continued inflow of dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Thursday between 35.850 rupees and 35.865 rupees, dealers said. It ended Wednesday between 35.850 rupees and 35.855 rupees at the close of interbank trading. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers expect the dollar to range between 35.84 rupees and 35.86 rupees for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market later in the day, because in recent days it has usually come in to buy dollars near the close of the session. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES INDIA REPORT 13-03-97 \par \par \uc2  0605GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt3d00guj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
