\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends steady, gains vs forward dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, March 12 (Reuter) - The rupee ended steady at 35.845/855 against the dollar in the spot market on Wednesday but gained against the forward dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the rupee gained to 35.83 around noon from 35.84/85 opening but reverted to the opening level after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupee saw its peak at 35.830 and its weakest point at 35.855 on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI continued to defend the dollar, buying both spot and forward dollars, they said. RBI bought spot dollars at 35.84. \par \par \uc2  In the forwards section, the RBI continued its outright purchases of May dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said RBI's total purchases on Wednesday could be as large as $100 million. \par \par \uc2  The RBI will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the rupee from strengthening but a resulting boost to monetary growth was a constraint, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said in an interview to Financial Express newspaper on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in response to a question whether the RBI would help exporters by encouraging a gradual depreciation in the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "I think this is one action we are taking," he said. \par \par \uc2  The forward premia looked up after RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The six month annualised premium closed Wednesday at 6.63 percent, up from the previous close of 6.47 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3c08sy5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
