\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Ends Lower On Heavy RBI U.S. Dollar-Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the rupee lower against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, erasing much of the gains the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  logged Monday in the wake of Friday's market-friendly budget statement. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that the dollar opened slightly lower Tuesday, as players continued to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Friday's budget, which convinced many players that foreign investment inflows will rise sharply in coming weeks and months. \par \par \uc2  But the Reserve Bank blocked the move by mid-afternoon, aggressively stepping in to buy dollars from a number of different banks, in at least four rounds at progressively higher levels. The moves lifted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders who dealt with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it began buying at 35.8350 rupees and continued up to 35.8750 rupees, buying about $5 million per transaction in dozens of trades. \par \par \uc2  A senior official of the Reserve Bank, who asked not to be named, also confirmed the dollar buying, reversing the bank's recent practice of declining comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities. He didn't confirm the rate or the quantity at which the dollars were being bought. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 GMT (5:30 a.m. EST) close of Bombay interbank trading, the dollar was quoted at 35.88 rupees, up from 35.8350 rupees Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-03