\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Steady On RBI Dollar Purchase \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1996\par 13:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee held steady against the dollar Thursday, as the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to block a decline in the dollar below current levels on good supplies of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid slack demand, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened higher around 35.85 rupees on some overnight short covering by traders, and rose to touch 35.87 rupees briefly, before emerging dollar supplies at current levels took the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower levels. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar hovered around 35.85 rupees in late morning trading before drifting lower to around 35.83 rupees on significantly less than usual demand from a major state-owned bank. \par \par \uc2  'There was a good amount of dollar supplies, and not much buying from the SBI (State Bank of India). (Dollar) sales through the day took the dollar gradually lower,' a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  The State Bank of India is the country's largest commercial bank and deals in the relatively small domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of some of the country's large private and state-owned companies. Its actions very often affect market trends. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the RBI entered the market around 0930 GMT to buy dollar for rupees around 35.835 rupees, blocking a further slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  An RBI spokesperson confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for rupees, but as usual declined to state the amounts or the level at which deals were done. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 GMT close of Bombay's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the dollar was quoted at 35.835 rupees, unchanged from late Wednesday's level. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1212GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscj01sse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
