\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Steady On RBI Dollar Purchases \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1996\par 14:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee held steady against the dollar Monday, as the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to block a decline in the dollar below current levels. \par \par \uc2  Traders said dollar inflows continued to put downward pressure of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as foreign institutional investor funds and telecom related inflows increased dollar supplies in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But the Reserve Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar by buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from some foreign banks during the day, as it has done in the past few trading days. \par \par \uc2  'The RBI was doing a mopping up \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' a trader at a foreign bank in Bombay said. He said the RBI had bought dollars at levels between 34.21 rupees and 34.22 rupees, helping to block a move below these levels. \par \par \uc2  'There has been a supply of dollars right through, but it increased around midday,' a trader with a U.S. bank said, noting that demand for dollars fell behind supply, bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in lots of $2 million and $3 million from a few foreign banks, traders said, adding that it was a routine \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  which didn't move the market significantly. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 close of Bombay inter-bank trading, the dollar was trading at 34.21 rupees, unchanged from Friday's late evening rate, and down slightly from the intra-day high of 34.24 in early trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1225GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4f036vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
