\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Stronger Despite Repeated RBI Dlr Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 13:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee strengthened slightly Tuesday despite repeated Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to block the rise in late trading, as dollar supplies outpaced dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly bought dollars around 34.10-34.11 rupees in afternoon trading, traders said, noting that although the volume of trade was quite large, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to reverse the dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  At the 1030 close of Bombay inter-bank trading, the dollar was trading at around 34.105 rupees, down from 34.13 rupees late Monday. \par \par \uc2  'Everyone seemed to be selling' dollars Tuesday, a trader with a European bank said, noting that as the dollar fell toward 34.10 rupees, sellers waited for the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a small boost, and then unloaded their holdings at a higher level. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar looks well-supported at these levels,' another trader with a European bank said, noting that the RBI was seen to be supporting an exchange rate of 34.10 rupees, while other players are also eager to buy dollars at that level. \par \par \uc2  But he noted selling interest remains strong at slightly higher levels, making range-bound trading likely for the next few days. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1214GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3q02o5b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex1