\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Edges Down After RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Blocks Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 12:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee fell slightly against the dollar Monday, after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) reversed an early rally. \par \par \uc2  Traders reported continuing heavy dollar sales in early trading, dropping the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a low around 34.04 rupees in morning trading, from late Friday's level of 34.09 rupees. \par \par \uc2  But the RBI emerged to mop up those dollars, buying dollars between 34.05 rupees and 34.10 rupees, traders who dealt with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. The buying pushed the dollar back to 34.10 rupees, where it traded for the rest of the local day. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably bought about $200 million during the day, judging by the amounts it bought at each bank. A spokeswoman for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it bought dollars, but as usual declined to comment on the levels or amounts. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued the RBI's recent strategy of buying dollars just above the 34.00 rupee level, apparently in an effort to block the dollar from falling below that point. \par \par \uc2  And traders predicted that the strategy would prove successful, as recently-strong foreign investment begin to slow down and demand for dollars from importers increases. \par \par \uc2  'I think it's going to continue like this for a week, and then the dollar will go back up,' a trader at a European bank in Bombay said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1141GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3b024im\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
