\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  RBI/Tarapore -4: Several Options On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 12:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Tarapore also noted that it is essential that \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy respond to changes in the external accounts, and said one aspect of that response was in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  'To support a sound macroeconomic policy, the exchange rate should be so determined that the trade weighted exchange rate remains stable in real terms, i.e. the exchange rate needs to be adjusted for inflation rate differentials,' Tarapore said. \par \par \uc2  He added that when the exchange rate does get out of line with economic fundamentals, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to respond with measures beyond direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'While this is one option, it cannot be a viable long-term solution. More effective \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be in the form of interest rate changes, reserve requirements and other tools of monetary policy.' \par \par \uc2  Despite a drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves over the past year, Tarapore said he expected foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets to be 'well over' $16 billion at the March 31 end of the fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets rose to $16.006 billion in the week ended Feb. 23, from $15.988 billion the week before. Total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which include gold and special drawing rights (SDRs), rose to $20.653 billion in the week, from $20.634 billion the week before. \par \par \uc2  He said India's liabilities to the International Monetary Fund would total SDR 1.6 billion at the end of March, down from SDR 3.6 billion in June 1993, adding that repayments to the fund would taper off in the next three years. And while noting that India would need to repay about $2.2 billion in the next fiscal year for a development bond, he said the current account deficit will still be 'sustainable.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1120GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3401xaw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
