\par\par \b \uc2  India's RBI/Forward Mkt -2: Traders Say Sold August Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1996\par 11:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (AP-Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, a spokeswoman for the bank said. \par \par \uc2  Traders who dealt with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold dollars for August delivery at a premium of around 3.25 rupees above the current spot market level. \par \par \uc2  They added that the sales depressed the August premium for a short time, down to around 3.05 rupees, but said the premium bounced back to 3.25 rupees at 1010 GMT after the sales were completed. \par \par \uc2  Although the RBI spokeswoman confirmed that the bank had sold dollars in the forward market, she declined to provide details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1010 GMT, the dollar was quoted in the spot market at 36.82 rupees, down from 36.95 rupees late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1021GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2d01ana\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
