\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee could fall to 40 per dollar - industry. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Verma \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 1996\par 07:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, Feb 7 (Reuter) - The Indian rupee could tumble to as low as 40 per U.S. dollar before coming general elections, triggering a slowdown in domestic investment, industry analysts said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It looks to me that probably it will touch 40," said M. Roy, a senior official at the Confederation of Indian Industry. \par \par \uc2  "This way, it is bound to affect project viability and many, many of our industries are going to postpone fresh investment because a lot of machinery and equipment are imported." \par \par \uc2  The rupee touched a record low of 38.35 per dollar on Tuesday, more than four percent below its opening level on Monday and 10 percent lower than at the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some ground on Wednesday on news Finance Minister Manmohan Singh and Reserve Bank of India (RBI) governor C. Rangarajan were meeting in Delhi to discuss the rupee's plight. \par \par \uc2  At mid-morning on Wednesday the rupee was trading at 37.55/65 per dollar, slightly stronger than Tuesday's close of 37.70/37.80. \par \par \uc2  Roy told Reuters the rupee's volatility was fuelled by speculative trading. \par \par \uc2  "Importers are bunching their demands while exporters are holding back their remittances, and such aggressive buying is causing a paucity of dollars," she said. \par \par \uc2  The Economic Times newspaper said Indian exporters failed to repatriate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings amounting to more than 70 billion rupees ($1.85 billion) in calendar 1995. \par \par \uc2  A rift between the Commerce Ministry and the RBI emerged on Tuesday when a senior ministry official accused the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of failing to do its job of checking the rupee's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, when the market is so volatile, the RBI should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively to ensure stability," said Roy. "Industry would like to operate in a situation of stability." \par \par \uc2  But V. Raghuraman of the Associated Chambers of Commerce and Industry of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ASSOCHAM) said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could only be a short-term solution. \par \par \uc2  "Unless we are able to improve our own productivity, the rupee will depreciate," he told Reuters. "Right from September, the industry has understood we have to look after our own interests and stop relying on the RBI as a crutch." \par \par \uc2  Until last August the rupee had held steady for two years at about 31.40 per dollar. But higher inflation in India than the United States took its toll, triggering a selloff in rupees. Between August and October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell about 12 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The RBI cannot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a big way for a lasting solution," Raghuraman said. "The only way to stop it is to beef up exports and attract more foreign investment to India." \par \par \uc2  He said Indian shares were currently selling at throwaway prices. "It's a very good buy for foreign investors," Raghuraman said. "When the rupee depreciates, it attracts foreign investment as our scrips are very cheap. \par \par \uc2  "But we must be prepared for the slide. It should settle maybe at 40 or even at 37, but there can be stability only after the elections," he added, referring to general elections which must be held by mid-year and are expected in April. \par \par \uc2  "The slide is a temporary phenomenon," Roy agreed. "It will continue for some time, for a month or so perhaps, until the elections." \par \par \uc2  Lehman Brothers analyst Arup Raha said the rupee could touch 40 per dollar if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to between 108 and 110 yen. On Wednesday the yen was at 105.75/85. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2701u8y\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (india near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbr